jobs.description:
A leading international pharmaceutical organisation in Berchem is looking for an Accountant to join their team. This full-time role offers the perfect mix of responsibility, variety, and professional growth within a supportive and international environment. With flexible working hours, attractive benefits, and a collaborative culture, this is your chance to make a real impact.

Your responsibilities as Accountant:

• A-Z responsibility of various VAT (BE + Other EU) declarations on monthly and quarterly basis;
• Assist the team in the daily operational accounting tasks (financial journals, purchase invoices,…);
• Back-up of other accountants;
• Cashflow-management (prepare foreign currency exchanges, ICO-payments, …)
• Preparing vendor payments in Isabel;
• Controlling and administrating the expense note application;
• Handling of the general finance mailbox
• Preparing and recording monthly accruals and deferrals;
• Assist in month-end and year-end closing;
• Assist in ad hoc projects to optimize current processes;
• The accounting team currently consists of 2 accountants.

Your profile as Accountant:

• Bachelor in Accountancy 
• First years of experience in similar roles
• Good knowledge of BE VAT
• Proficient in MS office
• Knowledge of MS AX and MS D365 is a plus
• Fluent in Dutch and English
• You are accurate and detail-oriented
• Proactive, stress-resistant, and eager to learn with strong analytical skills.

You’re an experienced SAP FICO consultant with a passion for helping finance professionals make the most out of their day-to-day jobs.

You make SAP implementations (both on premise and in the cloud) a success by thoroughly analyzing a company’s financial processes and by listening carefully to figure out what customers really need. You use your business knowledge and SAP expertise to question, explore and co-create new financial processes together with the customer.

You’re open, knowledgeable, and take on a pragmatic and transparent approach when it comes to finance and controlling requests. You put your previous experience in finance to excellent use to serve your clients. Are you ready to guide our customers through their finance journeys?



Your profile

• at least 4 years of SAP Finance experience (either as a consultant or as an employee);
• are very familiar with a wide range of Finance & Controlling topics;
• have previously delivered SAP implementations in finance. Any experience in integration with other modules (such as SAP MM or SD) is a plus;
• can carry out a blueprint analysis independently, but also know how to use your powers of persuasion to collaborate with fact-minded people;
• are open to sharing your expertise and mentoring more junior colleagues. Can we count on you to prepare the next generation of SAP FICO consultants?
• are eager to keep learning about the latest SAP S/4HANA innovations in finance;
• 
can fluently speak Dutch or French and English
